# BGE-M3 Multi-Vector Generation

Status: completed on 2026-09-07.

## Objective

Generate the official frozen BGE-M3 ColBERT token representation for every canonical resume and job description. Preserve token-level context for downstream interaction rather than collapsing each document to one dense vector.

## Reproduce

```bash { name=generate-multivector-cache }
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/ml"
.venv/bin/python scripts/generate_multivector_embeddings.py \
  --model-dir data/models/bge-m3 \
  --device cuda:0 \
  --batch-size 1
```

## Encoding Contract

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Model | `BAAI/bge-m3` |
| Implementation | `FlagEmbedding.BGEM3FlagModel` 1.4.2 |
| Representation | Normalized ColBERT token vectors |
| Model parameters | Frozen |
| Inference precision | FP16 |
| Cache precision | FP16 |
| Token-vector width | 1,024 |
| Context limit | 8,192 tokens |
| Excluded token | CLS |

For a resume with `n` retained tokens and a JD with `m` retained tokens, the cached representations are `R ∈ ℝⁿˣ¹⁰²⁴` and `J ∈ ℝᵐˣ¹⁰²⁴`.

## Validation

- A CUDA smoke test produced the expected 11 non-CLS vectors for an 11-token input.
- The smoke-test output shape was `(11, 1024)`.
- Token-vector norms ranged from `0.99999994` to `1.00000012` before FP16 cache conversion.
- The full cache contains all 643 resumes and all 351 JDs.
- Every document fit within BGE-M3's 8,192-token context; no truncation occurred.

## Corpus And Runtime

| Corpus | Documents | Token vectors | Minimum | Maximum | Runtime |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Resumes | 643 | 889,715 | 238 | 5,447 | 138.392 s |
| JDs | 351 | 202,846 | 18 | 1,771 | 32.451 s |

The run used an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Laptop GPU and Torch 2.6.0 with CUDA 12.4. The cache fingerprint is `4a9621f07c79b41eeef5b8f860d44f9643f5579318e92531c7a0ba823beb7756`.

